The mapping behavior appears unchanged, but the new diagnostics can produce false or stale selected-match reports for non-target networks. These are correctness issues for the diagnostic feature introduced by the patch.

Full review comments:

- [P2] Match only the intended benchmark names — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/base/abci/abcStmap_75.c:25-32
  For unknown designs whose network name merely contains one of these substrings, such as `decoder` containing `ode`, this assigns a benchmark-specific watch ID instead of disabling the diagnostic. Since AIG IDs are local to each design, `stmap75` can report `watched-aigs = 1` and log unrelated selected-match rows for unknown networks; compare against the expected benchmark basename/name instead of substring matching.

- [P3] Reset selected-match counters when disabling — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/map/mapper/mapperMatch.c:1597-1598
  If `stmap75` is run on an unrecognized network after a watched run in the same ABC process, this branch only clears the active count, leaving the previous row count, hit counts, and watch IDs intact. The summary printed for the unrecognized run can therefore contain stale rows/watch IDs even though watching is disabled; clear the counters and IDs on disable as well.
