codex
The build and default benchmark path appear to work, but the new diagnostic silently disables itself for the required i10 benchmark when invoked through common equivalent paths. This leaves a correctness gap in the diagnostic feature.

Review comment:

- [P3] Normalize i10 path names before watching — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/base/abci/abcStmap_75.c:25-26
  When the required i10 benchmark is read through an equivalent path such as `./benchmarks/i10.aig` or an absolute path, ABC names the network `./benchmarks/i10` (or the full path), so these exact comparisons miss it and `stmap75` disables the selected-match diagnostic with `watched-aigs = 0`. Since the command explicitly supports the i10 benchmark, normalize or strip path prefixes before matching instead of accepting only `benchmarks/i10` and `i10`.
